Research decision memo — Stage 6
Title: Minority Game and Strategic Financial Trading (Challet)
Status: NOT STARTED

Central hypothesis: Can contrarian strategic trading and price impact in Minority Game environments be represented as optimizing Nash or rational-expectations equilibria?

Feasibility prior:
Conditional: a congestion/strategic trading equilibrium may exist, but original adaptive score-update algorithms need not satisfy rational expectations; do not equate these two objects.

Core economic distinction:
Competitive rational portfolio choice with no strategic crowding; original adaptive Minority Game reported separately

Conditions to check:
1. Trader dynamic best responses/Nash conditions
2. Asset demand, inventory and security market clearing
3. Rational expectations for price mappings conditional on signals
4. Balance-sheet transfer and price impact identities

Pass / fail criterion:
Accept a game-theoretic equilibrium variant if it is nondegenerate; retain original adaptive dynamics only as a clearly labeled relaxation.

The project reports negative feasibility results when a kinetic, entropy, adaptive-trading, or heuristic-firm mechanism cannot be reconciled with optimization and equilibrium. Do not silently weaken rational expectations or drop clearing equations.

Evidence status: no derived theorems, numerical solutions or validated simulations committed yet.
